{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1019665-intimacy-system-in-cofd","id":1019665,"title":"Intimacy System in CofD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-20T02:10:04-08:00","id":1019665,"title":"Intimacy System in CofD","content":"So for those of you who don't know, the intimacy system is used in Ex3 for it's social system. Basically a character has Intimacies representing his opinions and emotional ties, they're a mix of vice, virtues, and aspirations. An intimacy has 3 strengths, minor, major, and defining. Minor intimacies are notable relations influence a character's action but not an integral part of someone. Major intimacies affect you life in many areas, and Defining, well, define your life.<br /> <br /> Now if someone tries to ask you to do something, barring magic and incredibly trivial task, is that you must use someone's intimacies to make them do it. You're not gonna make someone die for you by playing on their like of chilli peppers, unless he <i>really likes</i> those chilli peppers.<br /> <br /> Now you can give, strengthen, or erode intimacies but that's a relatively simple hack. The problem is I don't know how to give willpowers, beats, and the like.<br /> <br /> So any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11724-backtoback","name":"backtoback","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-20T03:44:46-08:00","id":1019688,"title":"","content":"Do you want Intimacies, per se, or do you want the Social Influence system? They're two different things.<br /> <br /> If you just want Intimacies, then I'd say drop Virtues, Vices, and Aspirations and replace them with Intimacies. You regain 1, 2, 3 points of Willpower for acting in accordance with your Intimacies, and that's limited to once, at all, per scene. If you act <i>against</i> your Intimacies, you gain a Condition of some kind that reflects this internal struggle, which inflict Breaking Points as the situation demands, and you resolve it by shifting your Intimacies around as appropriate. So your Intimacies indicate who you are; you're more capable when going along with this and rewarded accordingly; and you crash-and-burn when you go against it. I suspect that, to find the right balance, you'll have to drop Defining Intimacies.<br /> <br /> If you want the Social Influence system, then that's a whole other thing, because the Social Influence system is primarily about actually changing minds, which is a very small part of CofD (i.e., the Persuasion skill; notice that Exalted does not have that skill). So the question you have to answer first is, do you want a system where a win means the loser changes his mind, or do you want a system where a win means the loser grudgingly does what you ask them to do? The former is a lot easier, because you're just adding a system to the game and toolbox accepts more tools. It's then just a question of how kludgy you want the hack to be. The latter means trying to map things to Doors and that's really not easy because Intimacies are basically a rudimentary framework for describing a personality and CofD simply doesn't have that.<br /> <br /> (And speaking as a non-developer, the <i>reason</i> CofD doesn't have that is because Intimacies are an inherently outward-focused set of personality traits, in much the same way, say, CortexPlus Drives or Pendragon Traits are, and CofD is by nature a highly introspective, inward-focused system. Virtues, Vices, and Aspirations are justifications <i>to yourself</i> for what you do, whereas Intimacies are explanations <i>to others</i> for what you do... which is precisely what makes them manipulable. Also, being forced into a corner by your principles is a staple of an Eastern-origin genre like wuxia, but relatively uncommon in the Western canon where principles tend to be liberating forces that set the world afire in your name.<br /> <br /> ...but that's not what you're asking about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I call the Integrity-analogue the &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/822559-trying-to-understand-the-morality-system?p=825008#post825008\" target=\"_blank\">subjective stat</a>&quot;.<br /> An explanation how to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/913221-using-social-manuevering\" target=\"_blank\">use Social Manuevering</a>.<br /> Guanxi Explanations: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=787824#post787824\" target=\"_blank\">1</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/787518-the-mysterium-and-their-contribution-to-mage-society?p=788173#post788173\" target=\"_blank\">2</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/833863-mages-and-trading-favors?p=834531#post834531\" target=\"_blank\">3</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2758-errol216","name":"Errol216","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}